An abdominal circumference ultrasound displays a grayscale transverse slice of the fetal or patient abdomen with echogenic bowel and liver, fluid-filled darker regions
Abdominal circumference ultrasound images show a rounded, anechoic or hypoechoic central abdominal cavity encircled by a brighter echogenic rim;
Abdominal circumference ultrasound images show a rounded to oval cross-section with an echogenic outer rim, heterogeneous internal echoes representing soft tissues and fluid-filled structures
Abdominal circumference ultrasound images show a cross-sectional grayscale fetal abdomen with a rounded echogenic skin contour, central hypoechoic stomach and liver regions,
Transverse grayscale sonographic view shows a rounded fetal abdominal cross‑section with a smooth hypoechoic central area, echogenic bowel and ribs, and overlaid calipers or an elliptical trace;
Transverse fetal abdominal ultrasound shows a round-to-oval cross-section with bright echogenic skin margin and hypoechoic subcutaneous layer, internal mixed echogenic bowel and stomach bubble;
Transverse fetal abdominal ultrasound shows a round to oval cross-section with an echogenic outer skin line, concentric soft-tissue layers, relatively homogeneous liver echotexture,
Transverse fetal abdominal ultrasound shows a rounded, hypoechoic central cavity with echogenic liver and intestinal loops, a bright skin line and subcutaneous fat;
Grayscale axial ultrasound showing a rounded or oval abdominal cross-section with an anechoic stomach pocket, echogenic bowel and vertebral shadowing, and a measurement ellipse or calipers;
Grayscale transverse abdominal circumference images show an oval or round fetal cross-section with an outer echogenic skin line, variable subcutaneous brightness, internal speckled liver texture,
